messages:
jordan: Heads up — customer (Acme) hit a repeatable bug on our TS SDK running in Vercel Edge. Their app goes into a retry loop after a transient network error and we return 409 on the retried request. They provided a small repro.

acme_support: repro steps from our side:
1) deploy to Vercel Edge runtime
2) call the TS SDK streaming endpoint (responses.create with `stream: true`)
3) kill the connection mid-stream (we used Chrome devtools)
4) SDK retries automatically and keeps getting 409s 
Logs: `POST /v1/responses 409 - conflict: upload id already exists`

acme_support: snippet we used (edge runtime):
```ts
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });
export default async (req) => {
  const r = await client.responses.create({
    model: 'gpt-xyz',
    input: 'stream test',
    stream: true,
  });
  for await (const chunk of r) {
    // forward to client
  }
};
```

emma: thanks — which SDK version? and do you set an idempotency key?

acme_support: TS SDK 0.9.2 (edge build). We rely on SDK default idempotency. No explicit key.

ben-eng: possible root cause: the edge runtime doesn't have `crypto.randomUUID()` in some Vercel builds, SDK fallback was to a timestamp-based id. If two retry attempts overlap (client retries + SDK internal retry) they can collide and server sees duplicate upload id and returns 409. The SDK then retries again with the same id -> loop.

oliver-sre: can confirm similar symptom from internal flaky network test earlier. We saw `idempotency_key` = `ts-1678923456` repeated across retries.

emma: workaround for customers — set explicit idempotency key on create call until we ship a fix. e.g. `client.responses.create({...}, { idempotencyKey: crypto.randomUUID() })` in the edge handler (polyfill if needed).

acme_support: we tried setting a UUID from `uuid` lib in the edge bundle and that fixed it locally. Can you push a patch?

ben-eng: already on it. We have a patch that: (1) uses a tiny UUID polyfill for edge builds, (2) changes retry backoff to avoid immediate replay with same key, and (3) logs when falling back to non-random id. Planning release 0.9.4-canary.

deploy-bot: canary deployed to `canary/edge-retry-fix` at https://deploys.internal/redwood/edge-retry-fix — rollout scheduled for tomorrow. :rocket:

emma: QA notes — need a unit test that mocks absence of `crypto.randomUUID()` and verifies idempotencyKey uniqueness across concurrent retries. Also add a note in release notes for customers using old edge runtimes.

acme_support: thanks — can you provide a minimal upgrade note? Our platform team needs the change documented before we update production.

jordan: I'll draft a short upgrade note: 1) bump SDK to 0.9.4, 2) if you cannot upgrade immediately, set an explicit idempotencyKey per request, 3) if you see 409s after upgrade, ping support with `x-request-id` and the `idempotency_key` from logs.

emma: thanks. Closing loop once canary proves stable. :thumbsup:
